<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sandžak</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sanjak of Novi Pazar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sandžak is a historical region on the border of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and Montenegro, named after the Ottoman Sanjak of Novi Pazar. Its main towns include Novi Pazar, Pljevlja and Bijelo Polje, and much of its population is Bosniak Muslim. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> garrisoned part of it from 1878 to 1908, and in 1912 it was divided between Serbia and Montenegro.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sandzak.jpg" alt="Sandžak" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WikiEditor2004 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sandzak_region_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
